																		SCP-4531 — Silence encourages the tormentor, never the tormented.
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/yossipossi" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2199269); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2199269&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834639" alt="Yossipossi" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2199269)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/yossipossi" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2199269); return false;" >Yossipossi</a></span> <span class="odate time_1566381732 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Aug 2019 10:02</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4336434">
									

<div style="text-align: center;">
<blockquote>
<p><em>The persistence and escalation of anti-Semitic phenomena…[and that] far from having been eliminated, anti-Semitism is today on the rise in Europe. It appears in a variety of forms and is becoming relatively commonplace.</em><br />
–Parliamentary Assembly of the Council of Europe, Resolution 1563</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<p>This article is about ethics, and the rise of modern day anti-semitism.</p>
<p>Originally, this was a collaboration between myself, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/secretcrow" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3604422); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3604422&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1582877335" alt="SecretCrow" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3604422)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/secretcrow" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3604422); return false;">SecretCrow</a></span>, and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/plaguebearer" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4364963); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4364963&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1582877335" alt="plaguebearer" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4364963)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/plaguebearer" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4364963); return false;">plaguebearer</a></span>. The original concept was similar, but not exactly the same as the final draft. We eventually lost interest, and we moved on.</p>
<p>Recently, California tried to integrate an &quot;Ethnic Studies Curriculum&quot; for schools to help promote diversity and highlight the struggles of smaller groups that faced persecution. This would have been a great idea, if not for the fact that Jews were not only <em>not</em> mentioned, but were instead displayed in a negative light, primarily due to the State of Israel.</p>
<p>Along with hundreds of thousands of other people, I was outraged, especially considering how much my people and race went through all throughout history. Excluding us was almost like pointing a collective middle finger at us and telling us to fuck off. The course is being redesigned due to backlash, but the fact that it even <em>happened</em> is a major telling sign at the way Jews are seen in the modern day, not including many, <em>many</em> other things.</p>
<p>In my anger, I remembered the old 2018 draft I had with Crow and Plague. I scrolled to the page, reread what I wrote, and rewrote what I read. I calmed down later, went back, rephrased the crazed ramblings, and then finished it.</p>
<p>I'm not sure what compelled me to make the Foundation the way it was, but I feel like it best stands as an analogy — of what, you can probably fill in the gaps.</p>
<p>However, I will say that I always felt the concept of &quot;cold, not cruel&quot; was intrinsically flawed. There are no absolute goods, and there are no absolute evils.</p>
<p>Besides, what is cruelty, if it's for a good cause?</p>
<hr />
<p>Department of Tactical Theology Logo created by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aethris" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5158506); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5158506&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1582877335" alt="Aethris" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5158506)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aethris" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5158506); return false;">Aethris</a></span>.</p>
<p><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalashriver.jpg">river.jpg</a></p>

