			<div class="content" id="post-content-4337790">
									

<p>I don't typically break format unless I'm trying to convey something (4213 has no cusotm formatting, 4792 uses the threat level to subvert the reader shortly into the SCP), and that's no different here.</p>
<p>The intention of the large header, when I wrote this, was not to tell the reader &quot;prepare for an epic quest unlike any other!&quot; but rather to inform the reader (alongside the warning box, heavy redactions, and other minor details) that this anomaly is of great importance to the Foundation. Once the reader has this in mind, I envisioned it would help them deduce what exactly is behind the redactions, and why the Foundation is limiting information on a &quot;need-to-know basis.&quot;</p>
<p>I completely understand why you'd respond the way you would to seeing that large introduction though, and I'm sorry that the intro ruined the entire piece for you. I'll take this feedback into consideration when designing SCPs in the future. Thank you for clarifying your downvote!</p>
<p>EDIT: Minor typo I noticed, like, months later lol</p>

