			<div class="content" id="post-content-4425965">
									

<p>Ey I like this. This is a skip that the more you look into it, the more you enjoy the small details put into it. For such a small skip, its strangely compact with information.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I noticed that the number of pair of hands = number of deaths that person caused. Maybe the animal that the -2 instances take represents the crime as well? Fox for the sly, wolf for the brutal, mallards are notoriously rapey animals etc</p>
<p>The guy that killed the Foundation researchers had a body count of 31. 64 Hands appeared. One of them held a scale, I'm not quite sure what the appearance of those last two hands inquires, other than the fact this person will be judged for their actions.</p>
<p>The Mayor herself has spilled a lot of blood, she may have not specifically killed anyone, but her policies probably have.</p>
<p>And then theres the mysterious Project Tochacha and the Thaumiel status which puzzled me at first because why would the Foundation need to classify as Thaumiel status a small community that makes anomalies appear? But then I realized that the liquid itself is a thing that the Foundation would really appreciate to collect more of to interact with dangerous cognitohazardous anomalies. It doesn't know how to fabricate it, but it does know how to extract it.<br />
Project Tochacha is the procedure in which the Foundation has figured out how to weaponize a tradition meant to expose the sins of the inhabitants to themselves and to make themselves repentant, and the Foundation found a way to maximize the creation process of this liquid by instigating and promoting a perverse mindset in the community, akin to the serpent telling Eve to eat the forbidden fruit.</p>
<p>The last line can be interpreted in a number of different ways. Either the Project found out an even better way of harvest, which is to introduce a person who has indirectly caused a lot of blood on their hands to the anomaly for gallons upon gallons of juice.<br />
Either that or the Project received absolutely 0 liquid from this instance, which made them panic. Maybe the mayor is part of the Project and is the one explicitly perverting her community for the Foundation, which made the anomaly decide not to produce anything to attempt to disrupt the Mayor's mindset of harvest?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Either way, I enjoyed this one. +1</p>

